From: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mwlwifi: exclude QoS Null frames from 8864 TX aggregation

mac80211 client probes use QoS Null frames with normal ACK policy and
intentionally bypass A-MPDU processing. The 8864 transmit path includes
these frames in its aggregation stream lookup. If a stream for the same
station and TID is active, the Block Ack assertion fires and the probe
is dropped.

Exclude QoS Null frames from aggregation handling so they use the
normal transmit queue and ACK policy. Also avoid reading an LLC/SNAP
EtherType from frames that have no data payload.

Signed-off-by: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/hif/pcie/8864/tx.c b/hif/pcie/8864/tx.c
index 1e225fa..b49ac3e 100644
--- a/hif/pcie/8864/tx.c
+++ b/hif/pcie/8864/tx.c
@@ -659,11 +659,13 @@ void pcie_8864_tx_xmit(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 		u16 pkt_type;
 		struct mwl_sta *sta_info;
 
-		pkt_type = be16_to_cpu(*((__be16 *)
-			&skb->data[ieee80211_hdrlen(wh->frame_control) + 6]));
-		if (pkt_type == ETH_P_PAE) {
-			index = IEEE80211_AC_VO;
-			eapol_frame = true;
+		if (ieee80211_is_data_present(wh->frame_control)) {
+			pkt_type = be16_to_cpu(*((__be16 *)
+				&skb->data[ieee80211_hdrlen(wh->frame_control) + 6]));
+			if (pkt_type == ETH_P_PAE) {
+				index = IEEE80211_AC_VO;
+				eapol_frame = true;
+			}
 		}
 		if (sta) {
 			if (mwl_vif->is_hw_crypto_enabled) {
@@ -732,7 +734,8 @@ void pcie_8864_tx_xmit(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 
 	if (sta && sta->deflink.ht_cap.ht_supported &&
 	  !(xmitcontrol & EAGLE_TXD_XMITCTRL_USE_MC_RATE) &&
-	    ieee80211_is_data_qos(wh->frame_control)) {
+	    ieee80211_is_data_qos(wh->frame_control) &&
+	    !ieee80211_is_qos_nullfunc(wh->frame_control)) {
 		tid = qos & 0xf;
 		pcie_tx_count_packet(sta, tid);
 
